{
  "_README": [
    "Bedrock-isolated agent auth template for Cartograph.",
    "",
    "WHERE TO PUT THE ACTUAL FILE:",
    "  Copy this template to ~/.claude/settings.cartograph.json on the host that runs",
    "  agent_manager (the cartograph runtime — NOT this repo).",
    "  Path is referenced by the env var CARTOGRAPH_AGENT_SETTINGS_PATH which the",
    "  cartograph agent_manager reads at boot (see src/shared/config.py).",
    "",
    "  cp settings.cartograph.json.template ~/.claude/settings.cartograph.json",
    "  # then edit + replace the token placeholder below",
    "",
    "HOW TO FILL THE TOKEN:",
    "  Replace AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK below with a fresh Bedrock API key from",
    "  AWS console (Bedrock → API keys → Generate). Tokens are presigned and",
    "  typically expire in 12h (X-Amz-Expires=43200). When rotating, just",
    "  overwrite the value in the file and restart agent_manager — spawned",
    "  claude -p subprocesses pick up the new --settings on next wake.",
    "",
    "  Tokens START with the literal prefix 'bedrock-api-key-' followed by",
    "  the base64-encoded presigned URL. Keep the prefix when pasting.",
    "",
    "HOW TO ACTIVATE:",
    "  export CARTOGRAPH_AGENT_SETTINGS_PATH=~/.claude/settings.cartograph.json",
    "  cd src && python -u main.py",
    "",
    "  shared/config.py auto-loads the 'env' block of this file at import,",
    "  so model ids + bearer token + region all flow through. Real shell env",
    "  vars take precedence (file is a fallback).",
    "",
    "TO REVERT TO SUBSCRIPTION MODE:",
    "  unset CARTOGRAPH_AGENT_SETTINGS_PATH",
    "  # restart agent_manager — spawned claude -p uses the user's default",
    "  # ~/.claude/settings.json (subscription auth) when no --settings given.",
    "",
    "SECURITY:",
    "  This template is safe to commit (no secret). The real file at",
    "  ~/.claude/settings.cartograph.json contains a presigned URL embedding",
    "  AWS session credentials — never commit it, never paste into chat,",
    "  never persist in workspaces/ (which is gitignored anyway).",
    "",
    "MODEL ID NOTES (the [1m] suffix is the 1M-context inference profile):",
    "  Bedrock requires inference-profile IDs like us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7[1m],",
    "  NOT native API aliases like claude-opus-4-7. shared/config.py reads",
    "  ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_{OPUS,SONNET,HAIKU}_MODEL from this env block and",
    "  passes them to each spawned claude -p via --model.",
    "",
    "  To pin a specific Bedrock model id directly (overrides the env-derived",
    "  default), set CARTOGRAPH_MODEL_OPUS / CARTOGRAPH_MODEL_SONNET in this",
    "  same env block."
  ],
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS": "1",
    "CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK": "1",
    "AWS_REGION": "us-east-2",
    "AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK": "<PASTE_BEDROCK_BEARER_TOKEN_HERE — must start with 'bedrock-api-key-' prefix>",
    "ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL": "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6[1m]",
    "ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL": "us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7[1m]",
    "ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL": "us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0"
  }
}
